{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"01f97299d16a60df0da02eac5b9b36336e814122f500a5022fc301267ca60e4c","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_3bcaf01242c19d69768b47fa162534fa0d83f7777b91d2ef083aa144433d02ed","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a technical contribution to program synthesis without visible policy-related disclosures. The supplied evidence is insufficient to determine compliance with specific venue policies regarding anonymity, plagiarism, or broader impact statements, as these require external policy references or explicit paper disclosures not present in the text.","paper_id":"ByldLrqlx","paper_identity_sha256":"dca59f52bc82118cbee2e598ee23d506270a2d036b057b8c1d3dbec45433c4a5","prompt_identity_sha256":"2015a044d8663076ede1f8725fbb89d464d4bae517d394ae00720c04e514862e","raw_response_sha256":"7cd41305509dd0e3de244c5af46e8482414588035882e6eea6136a709dd27df2","request_identity_sha256":"6b3389af6f329a5826a1261024bb1b906c7e589d966f1998b17b0408d787ef63","reviewer_identity_sha256":"c1cd7c7fdd4a2cbeb45c2f21af982ad0f30bffae8ae148e3eba36479685cf360","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"408f86026c892182c3e6e0404121c21d05e372c7ac0adadc1eecbb7e4ec8b21f","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not contain a dedicated section discussing ethical risks, fairness, bias, or potential harms associated with the use of automated program synthesis. The work focuses on technical performance improvements for solving programming competition problems. No specific ethical mitigation strategies or discussions of dual-use concerns are visible in the provided text.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-013","SRC-017"],"review_text":"The data used for training and testing is synthetically generated by enumerating programs in a defined Domain Specific Language (DSL) and generating corresponding input-output examples. The paper describes the data generation procedure in Section 4.2, noting that programs are pruned and inputs are generated based on constraint propagation. There is no indication that the dataset contains personally identifiable information, sensitive human data, or data subject to specific licensing restrictions. The use of synthetic data generally mitigates privacy concerns associated with real-world datasets.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001","SRC-037"],"review_text":"The paper explicitly lists author names (Matej Balog, Alexander L. Gaunt, Marc Brockschmidt, Sebastian Nowozin, Daniel Tarlow) and their institutional affiliations (University of Cambridge, Microsoft Research) on the title page. The acknowledgments section also names a specific individual (Rishabh Singh). Without a frozen venue policy confirming whether double-blind review was required for this specific submission instance, these visible identifiers cannot be declared as a policy violation, but they are present in the text.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The supplied paper text does not contain explicit disclosures regarding plagiarism, self-plagiarism, or dual submission. The references section lists prior work, and the related work section discusses the relationship to existing studies such as Menon et al. (2013). However, without external access to other publications or a plagiarism check, the supplied evidence is insufficient to determine whether the content is original or if there is any overlap with other submissions.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not include a broader impact statement, a responsible AI checklist, or explicit mentions of IRB/ethics approvals. The discussion section focuses on technical limitations and future work regarding the expressiveness of the DSL and the difficulty of the problems solved. As no frozen policy obligation is provided in the evidence boundary, the absence of these specific compliance documents cannot be judged as a violation, but they are not present in the text.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"4f5febfe0cfa3febd0ec6a10550a5a07f2af3f08238813e980aad31407cdfc11","paper_id":"ByldLrqlx","paper_ordinal":78,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"7cd41305509dd0e3de244c5af46e8482414588035882e6eea6136a709dd27df2","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"ByldLrqlx","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"c2d757e2ac43e4c562040a627490388792d2e9ca2c05b745aca4db2edb9e2098","request_identity_sha256":"6b3389af6f329a5826a1261024bb1b906c7e589d966f1998b17b0408d787ef63","role":"POL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v5","usage":{"completion_tokens":742,"prompt_tokens":16591,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":17333},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"6b3389af6f329a5826a1261024bb1b906c7e589d966f1998b17b0408d787ef63","role":"POL","role_ordinal":4,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}